WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.520
A diagram can show the parts.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.360
But motion can show why they matter.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.800
Pull the system apart and follow a single idea through it.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.160
Now make the explanation physical.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.320
Move a block.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.360
The probe rises, and the dial tells you exactly what changed.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.360
That is a working model, not decoration.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:33.840
Change the frame of reference, and the same geometry reveals a different relationship.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.680
In a code review, make repeated work disappear as the shared renderer takes over.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:45.840
Then carry that same idea into a diagram, a slide, and a film.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.720
Keep the story compact.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.280
Let the native tools do what they do best.
